  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A collection of limited transposition is one a transposition already fixes." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Open Music Theory's `106-collections.md` tabulates Messiaen's modes by their" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// \"number of unique transpositions\": the whole-tone collection has two rather" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// than twelve, the octatonic three. The chapter then says the property is not" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the modes' alone — \"other subsets/supersets of these collections may also" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// have this property\" — and this file computes it for three of those subsets." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The count is not a fact about collections that needs a table. A transposition" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// is a group element, a collection is a point it moves, and the number of" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// distinct transpositions is the size of the point's orbit; what is left over" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// is its stabilizer, the transpositions that put the collection back where it" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// was. `std::algebra`'s `orbit` and `stabilizer` are those two functions, and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// nothing in either one knows what a pitch class is." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// **Where this stops.** The whole-tone and octatonic collections themselves —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// six and eight members at a division of twelve — cost more reduction steps" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// than `02-core-calculus.md` §4's budget allows today, so what is written here" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// are the three subsets that fit: the tritone, the augmented triad, and the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// diminished seventh chord, which the chapter's own sentence covers. The modes" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// are prompt 165's, and the code they will run is the code below." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Limited Transposition\"" },
